{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>And Leah conceived, etc. And she conceived again, etc.</b> I saw fit to pay attention to the order of the names, for it would have been proper to precede the removal of the hatred and afterward the cause of the love, yet she said in the first instance <b>this time my husband will love me</b> and in the second the removal of the hatred. Further, what was her intention in saying (Genesis 29:34) ״הַפַּעַם יִלָּוֶה״ — was he not joined to her previously?" "<b>Indeed</b> she is vindicated, may she rest in peace, because there preceded for her the statement concerning which she fell in her own eyes — that she was the portion of Esau. And even though she saw that she was married to Jacob, this matter did not justify itself in her heart, for she was his destined mate. Therefore, when she saw that a son was given to her, she said: surely it is because of HaShem's mercy upon her, on account of her not being loved — for the righteous fulfill the command of the Sages (Avot 1:6) to judge favorably. And therefore she always judged favorably, and it never entered her mind that she was hated, as I explained in the verse (Genesis 29:31) ״וַיַּרְא ה׳״ etc. — and her mind was not so, and this is the trait of the fortunate. Therefore, when a first son was given to her, she said that this comes to fill the lack, which is the love. And when she saw that HaShem added and gave her a second son, she said: in retrospect I was mistaken in what I thought — that I lacked nothing but love. For behold, HaShem heard — meaning, what I myself did not understand, that I am hated; therefore He gave two: one to remove the hatred and one to bring in the love. And therefore she said (Genesis 29:33) <b>Because HaShem heard that I was hated</b> etc. And when He gave her a third son, she said: from now on there is no explanation for the matter other than that this comes to teach that her marriage was not in a mistaken fashion but rather she is indeed his wife. And this is what she said — <b>this time</b> it is justified to be joined to her in the capacity of wifehood. For if the aspect were merely the removal of hatred and the granting of love on account of my shame, two sons would have sufficed; but now with three, it is a strong presumptive confirmation that I am his destined mate, and her marriage proceeded from HaShem." "<b>Further,</b> she intended in her saying <b>my husband will be joined to me</b>, that even at the time of her departure from this world she will not be separated from him, since she is his destined mate — as they said, their memory for blessing (Zohar Mishpatim 102a), that the mates are joined together in the supernal world continuously. And she stated the reason: that she had borne him three sons, and with three it is a strong presumptive confirmation that I am his destined mate." "Further, she foresaw in the holy spirit that four women would be wives to Jacob, and accordingly her share comes to three according to the calculation. And when a fourth son was given to her she said (Genesis 29:35) <b>this time I will praise HaShem</b>, for until now He had rendered her the justice she required, but this time it is nothing but the outpouring of His goodness, may He be blessed, and blessing for the abundance of goodness."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:45:21.943807093Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}